{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Shall hang over the back of the Tabernacle.</b> Rashi: to cover the two cubits that were exposed on the boards. Not the boards specifically, for the cubit of them was set into the sockets, and this is according to the baraita; but according to the tractate Shabbat, all the western boards were covered — only the sockets were exposed. And according to everyone, the goat-hair curtains covered also the western sockets, for the dignity of the Shekhinah. But to the north and south the sockets were exposed. Tanna of the school of Rabbi Yishmael: to what is the Tabernacle compared? To a matron walking in the market, whose train walks behind her. And the straightforward reasoning: the corner-edge wings of the curtains were spread open at the top, for if you do not say so, they would be lying on the ground."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:38.003898721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}